      "title": "About",
      "description": "Faculty Positions – Employment Skip to main content Go to Williams College Home Menu & Search use tab and shift-tab to navigate once expanded Search Williams Search Box Search Suggestions Type in your search terms and press enter or navigate down for suggested search results. About Overview Mission Fast Facts Governance Academics Areas of Study Course Catalog Academic Calendar Tutorials Graduate Programs Study Away Winter Study Libraries Experiential Learning & Community Engagement Pathways for Inclusive Excellence Admission & Aid Apply Affordability Financial Aid Tours Life at Williams Overview Bookstore Dining Housing Health Services Integrative Wellbeing Services Religion & Spirituality Students ▶ Alumni ▶ Parents & Families ▶ Employment ▶ Faculty & Staff ▶ Apply Visit Give Quick Links: Arts Athletics Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Campus Map Directory Events News & Stories Williams Email Employment Faculty Positions Williams College has one of the lowest student to faculty ratios in the country. The members of Williams College’s accomplished and diverse faculty are strongly committed to original research and artistic creation and to teaching undergraduates from a rich variety of backgrounds and experiences. They contribute to a vibrant liberal arts environment that values collegial exchange, interdisciplinary work, and pedagogical innovation. The Williams faculty is exceptionally large for a college of its size, producing one of the lowest student / faculty ratios in the country. In accordance with its stated commitment to building and sustaining an intellectual culture in which all faculty, students and staff can thrive, the college appoints its outstanding scholars, artists, and teachers from broad, inclusive pools of candidates, and supports the work of new and continuing faculty through a range of programs and initiatives. Open Faculty Positions 2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Arabic Studies Description The Gaius Charles Bolin Fellowships at Williams College are designed to strengthen and expand the professoriate by supporting scholars and artists whose research, teaching, and engagement contribute to inclusive and intellectually vibrant academic communities. Through sustained mentorship, professional development, and full participation in the intellectual life of the College, fellows are supported as they … Continue reading \"2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Arabic Studies\" more » 2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Asian Studies Description The Gaius Charles Bolin Fellowships at Williams College are designed to strengthen and expand the professoriate by supporting scholars and artists whose research, teaching, and engagement contribute to inclusive and intellectually vibrant academic communities. Through sustained mentorship, professional development, and full participation in the intellectual life of the College, fellows are supported as they … Continue reading \"2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Asian Studies\" more » 2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Biology Description The Gaius Charles Bolin Fellowships at Williams College are designed to strengthen and expand the professoriate by supporting scholars and artists whose research, teaching, and engagement contribute to inclusive and intellectually vibrant academic communities. Through sustained mentorship, professional development, and full participation in the intellectual life of the College, fellows are supported as they … Continue reading \"2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Biology\" more » 2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Classics Description The Gaius Charles Bolin Fellowships at Williams College are designed to strengthen and expand the professoriate by supporting scholars and artists whose research, teaching, and engage